Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:58:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] GPU: VICTORY_SHADOW_MIRROR=1 video-memory mirrors of
 title buffer copies (HybridGt, experiment)

CPU keeps the system-memory copy, the GPU works on a DEFAULT-heap mirror;
CPU changes are copied up before a submission, declared GPU-written
ranges down after it. Run13 (RTX 4070 Ti): works mechanically but the
title declares huge written ranges (its 174 MB heap, many times), so
~640 MB down and 240-350 MB up per world frame: 1500 ms/frame (run4:
1140) and still a device removal. Off by default; needs exact GPU write
tracking to pay off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
